  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scale up of malnutrition preventative services and access to safe and protective education for drought affected children and women</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this $2.5m UNICEF is to provide life-saving nutrition and to (re-)enrol IDP children in formal and non-formal education. To that end, UNICEF will screen 120,000 children under 5 for malnutrition and provide them with high energy biscuits, and train 150,000 pregnant and lactating mothers on best practices for infant and young child feeding. In addition, UNICEF and its partners will establish 60 temporary learning spaces and equip them with learning materials and appropriate water and sanitation facilities to enable 10,000 children to access education. In total, 270,000 people including 150,000 women and 62,400 girls, will be reached through the nutrition component and 10,000 children, including 5,000 girls and 5,000 boys, will be reached through the education component.</narrative>
  </description>
